Once these beds were the pride of Thalos; now the flowers are grey stalks
and the trees are bare, and thorny vines climb the temple wall and catch at
your ankles. The path curves away north and south, the temple doors stand
open to the west, and Main Street lies east. A howl rises and breaks off.
